WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.627
Much of a company's knowledge lives in folders that another system keeps up

00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:08.540
to date, such as nightly exports on an F.T.P.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.168
site.

00:00:09.168 --> 00:00:13.166
This video shows how a file source reads a folder on a schedule,

00:00:13.166 --> 00:00:17.850
and keeps an assistant's knowledge current, without anyone uploading a file.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:28.220
Documents that change often, such as handbooks, price sheets and product exports, go

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.810
stale when someone has to upload each new version.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.287
Often another system already writes them to a folder:

00:00:36.287 --> 00:00:38.813
on the site's server, on an F.T.P.

00:00:38.813 --> 00:00:40.645
site, or on an S.F.T.P.

00:00:40.645 --> 00:00:41.340
site.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:46.280
A file source reads that folder on a schedule, and turns each file

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.190
into passages that the assistant can search.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:55.600
Only new, changed and removed files are processed, so the knowledge follows the folder.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.764
Three pieces work together.

00:01:01.764 --> 00:01:07.360
A knowledge base index stores the passages, so the assistant can search them by meaning.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.436
A Files data source is the target:

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:13.750
the knowledge base that the assistant answers from.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.683
A file source is the reader.

00:01:16.683 --> 00:01:20.664
It has a connector for a folder on the server, an F.T.P.

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:22.334
site, or an S.F.T.P.

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.040
site.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:27.949
Then you choose the data source on a profile, and the assistant answers

00:01:27.949 --> 00:01:29.840
from the files, with sources.

00:01:34.118 --> 00:01:36.802
First, the knowledge base index.

00:01:36.802 --> 00:01:44.148
Open Search, Indexes, click Add index, and click Add on AI Knowledge Base Index for Elasticsearch.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:49.494
Enter an Index Name and a Name, and pick the Embedding deployment.

00:01:49.494 --> 00:01:52.880
It cannot be changed after the index is created.

00:01:53.339 --> 00:01:54.398
Click Save.

00:01:54.398 --> 00:01:59.380
Data sources, file sources and web crawlers all store their passages in an

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.999
index like this one.

00:02:05.221 --> 00:02:10.001
Open Artificial Intelligence, Data Sources, and click Add Data Source.

00:02:10.452 --> 00:02:13.911
In Available Source Types, click Add on Files.

00:02:13.911 --> 00:02:16.572
It is the target for file sources.

00:02:17.023 --> 00:02:23.676
Enter a Name, and choose the Destination index, the knowledge base index that stores the passages.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.363
It cannot be changed after you save.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:27.924
Click Save.

00:02:27.924 --> 00:02:32.600
The data source is listed, and waits for a file source to fill it.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.640
Open Artificial Intelligence, File Sources, and click Add File Source.

00:02:42.091 --> 00:02:48.261
In Available Connectors, click Add on File system, which reads a folder on the site's server.

00:02:48.712 --> 00:02:53.466
Enter a Name, and choose the Target File data source, the one you just made.

00:02:53.466 --> 00:02:56.772
Several file sources can feed the same data source.

00:02:57.226 --> 00:03:01.093
Keep Enabled ticked, so that the scheduled reading runs.

00:03:01.093 --> 00:03:05.646
Re-read interval is how often the folder is read again, in minutes.

00:03:05.646 --> 00:03:10.886
The site checks once an hour, so a shorter interval still runs at most hourly.

00:03:11.339 --> 00:03:16.696
Figures says whether the charts and pictures inside documents are described:

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.199
Auto, All or Off.

00:03:18.199 --> 00:03:22.314
Describing figures uses a vision model, so it costs more.

00:03:22.314 --> 00:03:25.189
The other fields can stay as they are.

00:03:25.642 --> 00:03:29.884
Folder is the folder to read, inside the file sources area that your

00:03:29.884 --> 00:03:32.463
technical team set aside for this site.

00:03:32.463 --> 00:03:36.132
Tick Include sub-folders to read the folders below it too.

00:03:36.585 --> 00:03:37.633
Click Save.

00:03:37.633 --> 00:03:42.685
The list shows the source with its connector, and Never run as its last run.

00:03:46.891 --> 00:03:51.026
To read the folder right away, open the Actions menu of the source

00:03:51.026 --> 00:03:52.461
and click Read now.

00:03:52.914 --> 00:03:57.332
After a moment, the Last run column shows what happened:

00:03:57.332 --> 00:04:02.534
how many files were found, ingested, unchanged, removed and failed.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:05.718
Here all three files were ingested.

00:04:05.718 --> 00:04:10.909
From now on, the schedule keeps the data source in step with the folder.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:20.839
For a file server, click Add on SFTP in the Available Connectors.

00:04:20.839 --> 00:04:26.740
Enter the Host, the Port, which is 22 by default, and the Username.

00:04:27.191 --> 00:04:32.313
Sign in with a Password, or paste a Private key and its Key passphrase.

00:04:32.313 --> 00:04:35.971
They are stored encrypted, and never shown again.

00:04:36.425 --> 00:04:39.379
Folder is the folder on the server to read.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:43.660
Files per listing caps how many files one listing takes on, and a

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.795
listing that could not finish removes nothing.

00:04:47.294 --> 00:04:48.426
The F.T.P.

00:04:48.426 --> 00:04:56.135
connector has the same fields, plus an Encryption mode, which can be Automatic, None, Explicit F.T.P.S.

00:04:56.135 --> 00:05:01.934
or Implicit F.T.P.S., and a Data connection of Automatic, Passive or Active.

00:05:06.125 --> 00:05:08.713
Now give the assistant the knowledge.

00:05:08.713 --> 00:05:13.225
Open the profile, open the Knowledge tab, and choose the data source.

00:05:13.681 --> 00:05:18.842
Restrict answers to retrieved data only keeps the assistant to your files.

00:05:18.842 --> 00:05:24.261
When nothing matches, it says so, instead of answering from general knowledge.

00:05:24.715 --> 00:05:30.459
Strictness is how closely a passage must match the question, and Retrieved documents

00:05:30.459 --> 00:05:32.820
is how many passages come back.

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:33.905
Click Save.

00:05:38.088 --> 00:05:40.688
Now ask a question about the handbook:

00:05:40.688 --> 00:05:44.588
how many days of annual leave does a full-time employee get?

00:05:45.039 --> 00:05:48.759
The assistant answers from the file that the file source read.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:53.840
Under the answer, the numbered sources show which file the answer came from.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:59.897
Create the index and a Files data source, point a file source at

00:05:59.897 --> 00:06:05.634
a folder, and the assistant's knowledge follows the files, without anyone uploading anything.

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:07.140
Thanks for watching.

